Godot Engine 4.7.1-stable (web export templates)
------------------------------------------------

The ten minigames under frontend/games-dist/ (built from minigames/) are
HTML5/WebAssembly exports made with the official Godot Engine 4.7.1-stable
web export templates. Each build's index.js, index.wasm and the audio
worklet scripts are part of Godot Engine.

Sources of the texts below, taken verbatim from the godotengine/godot
repository at tag 4.7.1-stable (commit a13da4feb8d8aefc283c3763d33a2f170a18d541):

  - Godot Engine licence: LICENSE.txt
    https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4.7.1-stable/LICENSE.txt
  - Third-party components bundled with the engine (FreeType, mbedTLS,
    zlib, ENet, HarfBuzz, ICU, libpng, libwebp, zstd, Brotli and others),
    with their copyright statements and full licence texts: COPYRIGHT.txt,
    copied unchanged to GODOT_COPYRIGHT.txt in this repository.
    https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4.7.1-stable/COPYRIGHT.txt

Shipping COPYRIGHT.txt under the name GODOT_COPYRIGHT.txt is the approach
the Godot documentation recommends for third-party licences
("Complying with licenses", godot-docs branch 4.7,
https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.7/about/complying_with_licenses.html).
COPYRIGHT.txt covers every component in the engine repository, so it is a
superset of what the web export templates actually compile in.

